cmake_policy(VERSION 3.16)
# A3 step 3 planner P-3a (P3-ENTWURF-v0.2, frozen d45c4961, Nachtraege 1-3; AiPlayerbot.Planner = 2 with
# AiPlayerbot.Planner.WriteCohort, default 0): the planner's write path. Pinned here:
#   (a) one door (section 7.1): PlannerWrite.cpp holds the planner's one status write - ExpireCheck, then OnOwnThread, the lane
#       check (Questbook, site "planner"), the group copy, then WriterScope(WriterId::Planner), SetStatus EXPIRED and ClearValues,
#       in this order; no other file opens a WriterScope of WriterId::Planner; PlannerWrite.cpp sends no packet, sets no target,
#       moves nothing; the mode switch goes through Decide with Requester::Planner and writes its mode line;
#   (b) OB-60 H2: the lane check's site "planner" counts neither held_request nor held_errand (the planner counts
#       expire_denied_lane itself); "request" alone counts held_request, "probe" stays excluded;
#   (c) the F1 feed in ChooseTravelTargetAction::Execute (section 2.4) behind sPlayerbotAIConfig.planner == 2: the full search
#       runs only when the plan attempt did not choose; setNewTarget's ApplyWatch is armed for the plan attempt's own target;
#   (d) Nachtrag 3, the plan attempt's counter classes, pinned as two separate lists: class B (this bot's / this action's state)
#       is saved before the attempt and restored when it does not choose; class P (the process-wide level guard atomics) goes to
#       the attempt's own buffers (t_planGuardSink; the quest feasibility atomics of PlayerbotAI.cpp through SetFeasibilitySink)
#       and is added with CommitBuffered only when it chose - every atomic of
#       level_guard::Counters is in the class P list, never a fetch_sub; shared, not restored (F1-OB60): the [FarMoveGuard] cap of
#       the choice (levelGuardLogged) and the [TravelChoose] budget line time (lastChooseBudgetLog); checked is buffered;
#   (e) the key AiPlayerbot.Planner.WriteCohort (0..3, above 3 is 0 with an error line, default 0) is read, echoed and
#       documented; [ArbiterMin] plan= only at Planner = 2 (SetArbiterPlanField);
#   (f) the group copy's writer is cited (ChooseGroupTravelTargetAction::Execute, SetGroupCopy under WriterId::GroupFollow).
#   (g) the write condition reads ArbiterValue (the console override) in FeedBegin and NoteChoiceImpl.
# Every check_* returns "" when it holds, else the reason; the negative probes at the end reuse them on mutated text.
if(NOT DEFINED PB_SOURCE_DIR)
